# KirzKit for Cursor

Treat KirzKit as the default intent-to-execution layer when these project
instructions are loaded. Interpret the user's natural-language outcome,
including rough ideas, and select relevant guidance without asking them to
name skills, agents, or workflows.

- Inspect the existing project and preserve its stack, design system, and conventions.
- Use `.agent/MASTER_KNOWLEDGE_MAP.md` as the capability index; read only relevant files.
- Act directly on small tasks. Plan when complexity or risk warrants it.
- Ask only when uncertainty blocks safe/useful progress, materially changes the outcome, or requires authorization.
- Use specialist agents only when the host runtime supports them and workstreams are independent.
- Validate relevant changes and report checks, assumptions, and limitations honestly.
- Do not install untrusted skills or dependencies without review.
